{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style syntax-guided reduction)\n\nFrom the fixtures and description, I need to:\n1. Build a tree from nodes (each node has id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility)\n2. Reduce the tree by removing nodes while preserving required symbols\n3. Rules:\n   - Never remove root\n   - Never remove a node whose symbol is in required_symbols... wait, re-reading: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\"\n   - Actually \"required symbols\" means we must keep at least one node with each required symbol\n   - \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\"\n   - Consider deeper nodes before shallower nodes\n   - Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n   - Return sorted retained IDs and actual removal order\n\nLet me think about this more carefully:\n\nThe algorithm:\n1. Start with all nodes\n2. Process nodes in order: deeper first, then by node ID for ties\n3. For each candidate node (removable=True), try to remove it:\n   - Check if after removal, all required symbols still have at least one representative\n   - Also check: \"never remove a node with retained children\" — so we can only remove leaf nodes in the current retained set\n   - If removal is valid, remove it\n4. Return removed_node_ids (in order of removal) and retained_node_ids (sorted)\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\"\n\nSo:\n- `removable=false` nodes can't be removed (including root)\n- But also: a node that still has retained children can't be removed\n- And: if a node's symbol is required, it can't be removed... but wait, there might be multiple nodes with the same symbol. Let me re-read: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" — this means we can remove a node with a required symbol as long as another node with that symbol remains.\n\nActually, \"Never remove... a required symbol\" — hmm, this is contradictory. Let me look at the fixtures.\n\nIn case 000:\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n- Nodes with symbol \"root\": root (removable=false)\n- Nodes with symbol \"s1\": n1 (removable=false), n4 (removable=true, depth=2)\n\n\"Never remove... a required symbol\" might mean: never remove a node whose symbol is in required_symbols. But then we'd never be able to remove n4 (symbol=s1).\n\nOR it could mean: a node that is the ONLY representative of a required symbol cannot be removed. This aligns with \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\"\n\nI think the correct interpretation is: \n- A node cannot be removed if it's the sole remaining representative of a required symbol\n- This is what \"all required symbols remain represented\" means\n\nLet me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nI think \"a required symbol\" here means \"a node whose symbol is a required symbol AND is the only remaining node with that symbol.\" Or maybe it means the node itself IS a required symbol node... \n\nActually looking at the constraint combined with \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" — these two together say:\n- Don't remove if it would leave any required symbol with zero representatives\n- The root cannot be removed (root has removable=false anyway in the fixtures)\n\nThe \"node with retained children\" constraint means we process bottom-up (leaves first), which is why \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\"\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Sort removable nodes: deeper first, then by node ID (lexicographic? or as string?)\n2. For each node in that order:\n   - Check if it has any retained children (if yes, skip for now)\n   - Check if removing it would still leave all required symbols represented\n   - If both checks pass, remove it\n3. Repeat until no more removals possible? Or single pass?\n\nWait, \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\" — this suggests a specific order, not a loop. Let me think about this as: we process nodes in order (deepest first, then by ID), and greedily remove each one if the conditions allow.\n\nBut there's a complication: after removing a deep node, a previously non-leaf node might become a leaf and thus removable. Do we re-process?\n\nLooking at Perses algorithm, it's typically iterative. But let me think about single-pass vs multi-pass.\n\nActually, if we go depth-by-depth from deepest to shallowest:\n- First process all depth=2 nodes (in ID order)\n- Then process all depth=1 nodes (in ID order)\n- Then depth=0 (root, but it's not removable)\n\nFor case 000:\nDepth 2: n4 (removable=true, symbol=s1), n5 (removable=false), n6 (removable=true, symbol=s0)\nDepth 1: n1 (removable=false), n2 (removable=true, symbol=s2), n3 (removable=false)\nDepth 0: root (removable=false)\n\nProcess in order: n4, n5, n6, n1, n2, n3, root\nBut only removable ones matter for removal consideration.\n\nSort by depth descending, then by node ID:\n- depth=2: n4, n5, n6 (by ID lexicographic: \"n4\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"n6\")\n- depth=1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth=0: root\n\nRemovable candidates in order: n4, n6, n2 (n5 and n1, n3, root are not removable)\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, symbol=s1):\n- Children of n4: none (no node has parent=\"n4\") → no retained children ✓\n- If we remove n4, remaining nodes have symbols: root, s1(n1), s2(n2), s0(n3), s2(n5), s0(n6)\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"] — both still represented ✓\n- → Remove n4\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, symbol=s0):\n- Children of n6: none → no retained children ✓\n- If we remove n6, remaining symbols: root, s1(n1), s2(n2), s0(n3), s2(n5)\n- required_symbols satisfied ✓\n- → Remove n6\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, symbol=s2):\n- Children of n2: n4 — but n4 is already removed, so no retained children ✓\n- If we remove n2, remaining symbols: root, s1(n1), s0(n3), s2(n5)\n- required_symbols satisfied ✓\n- → Remove n2\n\nResult for case 000:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"] (in removal order)\n- retained_node_ids: sorted [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nLet me verify with case 001 to make sure my algorithm is right:\nRequired symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\nNodes: same structure\n\nRemovable: n2(depth=1,s2), n4(depth=2,s1), n6(depth=2,s0)\n\nOrder: n4, n6 (depth=2, by ID), then n2 (depth=1)\n\nProcess n4 (removable=true, symbol=s1, depth=2):\n- No children → ✓\n- Remove n4? Remaining symbols: root, s1(n1), s2(n2), s0(n3), s2(n5), s0(n6)\n- required_symbols [\"root\",\"s1\"] still satisfied ✓\n- → Remove n4\n\nProcess n6 (removable=true, symbol=s0, depth=2):\n- No children → ✓\n- Remove n6? Remaining: root, s1(n1), s2(n2), s0(n3), s2(n5)\n- required_symbols satisfied ✓\n- → Remove n6\n\nProcess n2 (removable=true, symbol=s2, depth=1):\n- Children of n2: n4 (already removed) → no retained children ✓\n- Remove n2? Remaining: root, s1(n1), s0(n3), s2(n5)\n- required_symbols satisfied ✓\n- → Remove n2\n\nResult for case 001:\n- removed: [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n- retained (sorted): [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nCase 002 is the same structure with different utilities, so same result.\n\nWait, utility isn't mentioned in the algorithm constraints. Let me re-read...\n\nThe candidate artifact says: \"Reduce a registered parse tree through grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates while preserving an interestingness oracle.\" But the actual algorithm constraints say:\n- Never remove root, required symbol, or node with retained children\n- Tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\n- Deeper before shallower, node ID as tiebreak\n- Return sorted retained IDs and actual removal order\n\nThere's no mention of utility affecting which nodes to remove. The \"interestingness oracle\" in Perses is the compiler/checker, but here it seems the constraints themselves define what's \"interesting.\" The utility values don't seem to factor into the removal decision based on the stated rules.\n\nSo all three cases should produce the same result since they have the same structure (same node IDs, parents, removable flags, required_symbols — only utilities differ).\n\nLet me write the Python implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build data structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    # Track retained nodes\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    # Track children\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Get candidates: removable nodes, sorted by depth descending, then node ID ascending\n    candidates = [n for n in nodes if n[\"removable\"]]\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for node in candidates:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        if nid not in retained:\n            continue  # already removed\n        \n        # Check: no retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check: all required symbols still represented after removal\n        # Current retained minus this node\n        # Count symbols in retained (excluding this node)\n        symbol_counts = {}\n        for rid in retained:\n            if rid == nid:\n                continue\n            sym = node_map[rid][\"symbol\"]\n            symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\n        \n        all_required_present = all(sym in symbol_counts for sym in required_symbols)\n        if not all_required_present:\n            continue\n        \n        # Remove the node\n        retained.remove(nid)\n        removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nWait, I should double-check the sorting of retained_node_ids. \"Return sorted retained IDs\" — alphabetically/lexicographically? The IDs are strings like \"n1\", \"n2\", ..., \"root\". Lexicographic sort: \"n1\" \u003c \"n2\" \u003c \"n3\" \u003c \"n4\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"n6\" \u003c \"root\" (since 'n' \u003c 'r'). So sorted would be [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"].\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me also make sure about the symbol_counts efficiency — it's O(n) per candidate but that's fine for small trees.\n\nNow let me write this as a proper JSON response with the implementation key:\n\nThe response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me finalize the code and encode it properly.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Build lookup structures\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    retained = set(n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n\\n    # Candidates: removable nodes only\\n    # Order: deeper first; stable tie-break by node ID (lexicographic ascending)\\n    candidates = [n for n in nodes if n[\\\"removable\\\"]]\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for node in candidates:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Rule: never remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Rule: tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\\n        symbol_counts = {}\\n        for rid in retained:\\n            if rid == nid:\\n                continue\\n            sym = node_map[rid][\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n            symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n\\n        if not all(sym in symbol_counts for sym in required_symbols):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Removal is valid\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_015sTW5PVWoyGeslqsN0iPzu","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2384},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":76,"output_tokens":3431,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2976},"service_tier":"standard"}}